Here is some sample Python code using the HipChat API and the Giphy API to get you started:
```python
import requests

# HipChat API settings
hipchat_token = "your_hipchat_token"
hipchat_room_id = "your_hipchat_room_id"

# Giphy API settings
giphy_api_key = "your_giphy_api_key"

def send_gif(message):
    # Search for a GIF using the Giphy API
    giphy_response = requests.get(f"https://api.giphy.com/v1/gifs/search?q={message}&api_key={giphy_api_key}")
    gif_url = giphy_response.json()["data"][0]["images"]["original"]["url"]

    # Send the GIF to HipChat using the HipChat API
    hipchat_response = requests.post(
        f"https://api.hipchat.com/v2/room/{hipchat_room_id}/message",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {hipchat_token}"},
        json={"message": gif_url}
    )

# Example usage:
send_gif("hello")
```
Note that this code is just a starting point and will require modification to fit your specific use case. You'll need to replace the placeholders with your actual API tokens and room IDs. Additionally, you may want to add error handling and other features depending on your requirements.
